problem_statement:
Derive formulas and calculate the values of the following quantities for the Moon. Use the definitions and data below, and report numerical results in SI units. Definitions: G is the universal gravitational constant, M is the mass of the Moon, R is the radius of the Moon, m is the mass of a test body at the Moon's surface, g is the gravitational acceleration at the Moon's surface, v_0 is the escape velocity from the Moon, E is the total mechanical energy of the projectile, U(ρ) is the gravitational potential energy at radial distance ρ from the Moon's center, and ρ is the radial distance from the Moon's center. Numerical data to use: G = 6.67×10^{-11} \unit{m^3/(kg s^2)}, M = 7.35×10^{22} \unit{kg}, R = 1.74×10^{6} \unit{m}

a) the gravitational acceleration at the surface of the Moon

b) the escape velocity from the Moon.
